{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews"]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" product to the test target. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"type":"text","text":" binds a fresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker to the test’s task for the length of its body, then returns every event tracked in it, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order. Here "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SignedUp"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["import Testing","import TrackerTesting","","@Test func signingUpTracksThePlan() async {","    let tracked = await withRecordingTracker {","        Tracker.current.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))","    }","    #expect(tracked.events(of: SignedUp.self) == [SignedUp(plan: \"pro\")])","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call has a tracker of its own, so tests running at the same time never see each other’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events. The body may be sync or async, and may return a value, read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.value"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.names"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every event’s name and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracked.records"},{"type":"text","text":" every record."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Most code needs nothing more: it tracks through ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which falls back to the tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the app bootstrapped, and the test’s binding wins over that one. A view whose tracker was never set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that binds its tracker with ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reaches the test’s tracker too. Pass a tracker instead where the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"code reads one set for a single view tree. A tracker given to a SwiftUI view with ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracker(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", such as a preview’s,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reaches the view’s environment but not code that reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker.current","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Such a test takes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker the body is given and sets it on the view: ","type":"text"},{"code":"withRecordingTracker { tracker in … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://TrackerTesting/documentation/TrackerTesting":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTe